# Notification policy (Mastodon's filtering). Reading it is the one row; an update reads it and
# upserts. A notice someone caused reads the type preference, the policy and the sender facts
# (permission, follows both ways, account age, private mention) in the one statement that used to
# read only the preference, so a follow kept aside is the plain follow minus the push lookups and an
# accepted sender's is exactly the plain follow. The list and unread count leave kept notices out in
# the same statement.
